<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovak Jan C/A deficit revised to $221.9 mln.</title>
<headline>Slovak Jan C/A deficit revised to $221.9 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) on Wednesday revised the country's January current account deficit to $221.9 million, from a previously announced $230.3 million.</p>
<p>Its latest monthly monetary survey obtained by Reuters on Wednesday said the capital account recorded a surplus of $209.1 million in January 1997. This entailed no revision from its original report.  </p>
<p>  SLOVAK CURRENT ACCT    Jan 97	   FY/96	Jan 96</p>
<p>  overall ($ million)   -221.9(-230.3) -1,940.8	 -19.6</p>
<p>  trade balance	   -219.3	   -2,105.8	 -50.2</p>
<p>  balance of services     +1.0		 +7.4	 +11.5</p>
<p>  income balance	    -9.6		-44.7	  +9.0</p>
<p>  current transfers	 +6.0	     +202.3	 +10.1</p>
<p>CAPITAL ACCOUNT</p>
<p>  Total balance	   +209.1	   +2,143.8	 -36.4</p>
<p>  capital transfers	  0.0		+29.7	   0.0</p>
<p>direct foreign</p>
<p>  investment		  -2.1	     +142.8	  +9.3</p>
<p>portfolio investment</p>
<p>  balance		     -7.1		 +9.0	  +9.0</p>
<p>net long and medium-term</p>
<p>  financial account	 -6.2	     +997.8	   n/a</p>
<p>net short-term fin.</p>
<p>  account		   +215.3	     +919.9	   n/a</p>
<p>Note. All figures are in millions of U.S. dollars and subject to revision. Figures in the brackets are those which have been revised from an original central bank report. The central bank used the following exchange rates in calculating the figures: USD=32.24 SKK</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-521-8402</p>
